        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Strongest Man in the World, Roving Mars, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell\n- Organizations: Disney\n- Places: Medfield College, Mars\n- Systems: Mars Exploration Rovers, Spirit, Opportunity\n- Topics: film sequels, documentary filmmaking\n\nFacts:\n- \"The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\" is a 1969 film.\n- \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't\" is a sequel to the 1969 film \"The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\".\n- \"The Strongest Man in the World\" is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell.\n- In \"The Strongest Man in the World,\" Kurt Russell plays a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- \"Now You See Him, Now You Don't\" was followed by the 1975 film \"The Strongest Man in the World\".\n- \"Roving Mars\" is an IMAX documentary film about the development, launch, and operation of the Mars Exploration Rovers.\n- The Mars Exploration Rovers in \"Roving Mars\" are Spirit and Opportunity.",
